{"duration_api_ms":169108,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4666583c-7ce2-47aa-a965-1bddf6eae563","total_cost_usd":1.1506222,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":58029,"cache_read_input_tokens":1905431,"output_tokens":15254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2206},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":58029,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":88926,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1441},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":56,"outputTokens":15254,"cacheReadInputTokens":1905431,"cacheCreationInputTokens":58029,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1506222,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2206,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":58029,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I finished PKT-0132 and committed it in both repos. Both acceptance checks pass, scope-check is clean (rule R2) and `theseus validate` reports no errors. The speed gain is still not proven, though: I measured on a busy VM, and the improvement is smaller than the run-to-run spread.\n\n**Recovery.** The previous attempt's main-repo work was missing and `external/web-apps` was back at upstream. I cherry-picked the two Comments/Toolbar commits from `fork/pkt/PKT-0132`. The PKT-0112 deferral comes with them, since that packet is blocked and its change wasn't on this branch. I took `perf/open-window-build.js` from `d926db4`.\n\n**Lock bug from the review.**\n- The add button was already being added to `lockControls` and `paragraphControls` when it got wired late, so that part of the rejection was handled.\n- When I tested it after load, a second bug showed up: the Comments panel's add button stayed disabled while the toolbar's comment button was enabled. The cause is that `ButtonsArray.add` applies the button set's own disabled flag, which is still \"disabled\" from start-up.\n- Fix in `Toolbar.js`: after adding the button, copy the locks and the disabled state from the toolbar's comment button.\n- I added `perf/comments-addnew-locks.cjs` to check this. With the fix, the button behaves exactly like the upstream build after load, and when connection-lost and paragraph locks are turned on and off.\n\n**When the panel gets built.** When the document finishes loading (`isDocumentLoadComplete`), the Comments panel isn't built yet. An idle callback builds it after `app:ready`, so the build no longer runs in the open window.\n\n**Measurement.** I compared upstream (A) against this branch (B) over 16 pairs of runs on each of two documents, alternating the order. Deltas are B − A, also written to `baseline.md`:\n\n| | Median change | Runs faster | Spread (IQR) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ready | −84 ms | 20 of 32 | −252 to +286 ms |\n| LoadDoc | +2 ms | 16 of 32 | — |\n\nLoadDoc wasn't expected to move, because the Toolbar wiring runs after it. The VM's load average was 3.4–6.0 the whole time because other factory agents were running. The reviewer asked for an idle VM and I couldn't get one, so that part of the rejection is still open. I said so in the Executor log and the friction line.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- A button added to a button set after start-up has to be re-synced from a sibling button, because the set forces its stale disabled flag onto it.\n- Performance A/B runs need an idle slot from the factory. With other agents running in parallel, the run-to-run spread is wider than a ~100 ms effect.","ttft_ms":3555,"type":"result","duration_ms":1068440,"uuid":"70b1964d-c7a5-4871-8a97-9a51e8e1754d","ttft_stream_ms":2213,"time_to_request_ms":251,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":139,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":9,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":19,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":26,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":148,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":243,"process_anon_mib_result":152,"process_peak_rss_mib":271,"process_cpu_ms_turn":8686,"process_wall_ms_turn":1068439,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2070,"process_wall_ms_streaming":121593,"main_stream_count":28,"main_stream_event_count":2156,"main_stream_chunk_count":1559,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":2070,"wall_ms":121593,"entries":28},"tool":{"cpu_ms":5002,"wall_ms":898684,"entries":27},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":922,"wall_ms":47391,"entries":28},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":149,"wall_ms":251,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":530,"wall_ms":499,"entries":27},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":13,"wall_ms":21,"entries":1}},"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":9,"cpu_ms":22,"